      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# DramaBox - Expressive Scene TTS and Native Timing Control\n\nDramaBox is an English expressive TTS engine designed around scene-style prompting.\n\nIt supports:\n\n- quoted dialogue\n- stage directions outside quotation marks\n- laughter, sighs, pauses, and delivery transitions\n- optional reference-audio voice cloning\n- native generation-duration targeting\n- CFG and negative prompting\n\nIt behaves like other TTS engines in the suite:\nconnect the Engine to the unified `TTS Text` or `TTS SRT` nodes and generate.\n\nDramaBox is officially **English-only**.\n\nIt does **not** support `🔄 Voice Changer`.\n\nReference audio is optional and does not require matching reference text. The `reference_duration` setting controls how many seconds are used from the beginning of the reference.\n\nDramaBox works best with scene-style prompts:\n\n- Put intended dialogue inside quotation marks\n- Keep delivery descriptions and stage directions outside quotation marks\n- Use the prompt template to automatically wrap plain segments as dialogue\n\nExample:\n\n`A tired narrator speaks softly, \"I thought this night would never end,\" then sighs.`\n\nDramaBox supports native duration targeting through `generation_duration`. In `TTS SRT`, subtitle durations can be passed directly to the model before the selected timing mode applies any final correction.\n\nThis makes DramaBox especially useful for:\n\n- expressive dialogue and narration\n- duration-controlled generation\n- SRT workflows requiring accurate segment lengths\n- reducing waveform stretching and compression\n\nDramaBox can be sensitive to reference audio, reference duration, requested generation duration, guidance settings, and seed. Some combinations may produce near-silent output. The suite reports affected segments so you can adjust those parameters.\n\nThe `staged`, `sequential`, FP8, and compile options are experimental performance and memory controls. Start with the default settings unless you need to reduce peak VRAM."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
